WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:11.509 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  these are the only survivors  of an air strike which killed most of  the majali family  the attack pretty much leveled their  home but the accounts of what happened  by the sole survivors  and the many witnesses we interviewed  have made the saudi coalition's position  unsustainable  after months of delay the coalition has  admitted they made a mistake  they bombed the wrong house  these inhospitable mountains were where  the majali family lived  now thrust into the front line of a  civil war that's tearing their country  apart  we've put together the most detailed  account yet about the massacre that  happened here  it's an attack which has now led to a  rare admission  by the saudi-led coalition that they  were responsible  for wrongly killing nine innocent  civilians  we found from the missile here's what  our investigation found out about that  airstrike  washer is close to the saudi border with  several air bases nearby  king khalid is closest making it the  most likely based the jet left from  it flew over the village for about an  hour starting around noon time on july  12  2020 12 members of the majali family  were in and around their single story  modern stone home  and it had six rooms mrs jumma majali  was making lunch with her two  daughters-in-law  nawal and noora about an hour later they  served the meal  and called the eight children together  to eat in the living room  her teenage daughter nasim left to the  bathroom and daughter-in-law nourah  went to a bedroom to breastfeed her baby  kanas mrs majali's teenage son ghazi was  watching tv next door  when the missile struck at ten past one  all those in the living room were killed  so was naseem in the bathroom  only teenage ghazi in one of the back  bedrooms  survived but was badly burned alongside  nora and her baby  who had minor wounds because they too  were at the rear of the house  in all nine of them died that day  we were the first journalists and the  only outsiders to reach the site of the  attack  several weeks after it happened  we gathered a pile of evidence and sent  our team  back to get more  the only survivors now live hundreds of  kilometers away but we tracked them down  i was screaming for help i was in shock  she says the house was destroyed i was  searching for my daughter but she was  dead  then i saw my sister-in-law and she was  dead too i just picked up my son  and screamed for help  mrs majali's teenage son ghazi is in a  separate home again far away  he can't remember much but his cousins  can  we only recognize his mother from her  torso  that was all that was left of his mother  he only managed to identify  one of the small children from his face  it was his brother's son his arms were  cut off  and his sister-in-law she had no leg and  no arm  and she was totally burned  it struck us then how remote the house  was despite claims from the coalition  about a possible military target there  everywhere you look around here there  are small farms there's little  residential clusters there's  homes and mountains it's very difficult  to see  what around here could be conceived of  as a legitimate  military target  yemen's been embroiled in a civil war  for the last five years  on one side as a coalition of nations  led by saudi arabia and backed by  britain  the u.s and the uae they're fighting  houthi rebels who control most of the  north with the support of iran  the conflicts created the world's worst  humanitarian crisis  we filmed some of the millions suffering  from malnutrition and disease  in yemen's most desperate areas when we  were last there  [Music]  since our reports the uns investigated  the bombing as a possible war crime  the coalition would have been aware of  this and ahead of us broadcasting these  fresh details  admitted they'd made a mistake  there was a military target they say but  it was nearly  800 meters away in the completely  separate area of bait al qasim  and they blamed poor weather in a  statement they said  the joint forces believed that the bomb  did not hit the target due to  intermittent clouds over the target area  15 seconds after the bomb was fired  which impacted the response of the  laser-guided bomb before landing on the  military target  these details emerge as the political  landscape is dramatically changing with  the new american president  already re-examining u.s arms sales to  saudi arabia  and the uae the british government may  also be forced to reconsider its  involvement in this war  alex crawford sky news

